The C# backend now writes every Dafny identifier that is a C# keyword as a verbatim identifier (`@name`). It escaped only some of them, so, for example, a parameter named `protected`, or a type named `record`, `file`, `required` or `scoped`, produced C# that did not compile. The backend now escapes all 77 reserved and all 46 contextual keywords of the C# language reference.
